# Twisted automorphic descents: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs whenever their
carriers exist or need only a few simple definitions. None of the following
headlines is statable on those APIs.

- Section 1.3, First-occurrence cuspidality: lacks automorphic realizations on
  SO(V) or U(V) over a number field and their rational Bessel coefficient maps.
- Section 1.4, Multiplicity-free Bessel decomposition: lacks those Bessel images
  and the discrete cuspidal Hilbert spectrum with specified central character.
- Section 1.4, Orthogonal local Bessel uniqueness: lacks smooth admissible and
  Casselman–Wallach local representation categories and continuous Bessel Hom.
- Section 3.4, Unramified Bessel integral calculation: lacks classical-group local
  zeta integrals, their smooth induced sections and parameter L-factors.
- Section 3.5, Tempered local factors and ramified normalizers: lacks the actual
  local standard modules and their tensor and signed-Asai L-factors.
- Section 3.6, Open-cell local nonvanishing: lacks these local zeta integrals and
  holomorphic smooth families in the local induced representation categories.
- Section 4.3, Maximal pole and central L-value: lacks classical-group Eisenstein
  families, their Laurent operators and completed GL tensor and type L-functions.
- Section 4.5, Holomorphy at the critical point: lacks the normalized Bessel zeta
  integrals and completed parameter L-ratios of those Eisenstein families.
- Section 4.6, Reciprocal nonvanishing of Bessel periods: lacks cuspidal
  realizations, Bessel periods and the leading residual automorphic module.
- Section 4.7, Nonzero period implies nonzero central value: lacks cuspidal
  realizations on SO(V) or U(V), Bessel periods and completed GL tensor L-functions.
- Section 5.2, Residual square integrability and membership in Arthur packets:
  lacks residual automorphic realizations, their Hilbert spectrum and Arthur packets.
- Section 5.4, Vanishing above the critical index: lacks residual Arthur packet
  members and their rational Fourier maps and twisted Jacquet modules.
- Section 5.5, Cuspidality at the critical index: lacks critical Bessel images in
  the classical-group cuspidal spectrum and residual cuspidal-support data.
- Section 5.6, Outer stability of critical Bessel modules: lacks those actual
  automorphic realizations and their rational Fourier images.
- Section 5.7, Unramified parameter of the critical module: lacks local residual
  representations, twisted Jacquet modules and their standard Satake parameters.
- Section 5.8, Structure of the critical cuspidal module: lacks critical Fourier
  images, the cuspidal Hilbert spectrum and global Arthur parameter assignments.
- Section 6.3, Known Fourier-support cases: lacks actual residual modules and
  their rational nilpotent Fourier-support sets.
- Section 6.4, Central value produces a global period: lacks coherent automorphic
  packets, their cuspidal realizations, Bessel periods and GL tensor L-functions.
- Section 6.5, Odd orthogonal–torus period criterion: lacks these coherent packets,
  Bessel periods and GL tensor L-functions, including for a simple parameter.
- Section 7.2, Cuspidal module recovery theorem: lacks actual twisted descent
  modules, enhanced local packets and cuspidal automorphic realizations.
- Section 7.3, Recovery from a regular Fourier coefficient: lacks those modules
  and their rational regular Fourier maps, including the smaller U₁ datum.
- Section 7.4, Generic summand from subregular support: lacks rational automorphic
  Fourier support, cuspidal Bessel images and global parameter assignments.
- Section 7.5, Recovery from subregular support: lacks those support sets,
  twisted descent modules and enhanced local packets.

Sections 2.2–2.4 and 3.2 are intermediate unfolding targets in README.md.
The rational isotropic-flag geometry of Section 2.3 needs no Eisenstein carrier;
its quadratic subspace invariants can be expressed with native quadratic forms.
It is not an automorphic headline. Section 4.7 itself needs no Eisenstein operator
in its statement.

Native partitions, algebraic representations and meromorphic scalar functions
do not supply the missing automorphic carriers. Arithmetic identities, scalar
period witnesses and boundary computations remain README Checks. No missing
condition is encoded by an arbitrary predicate or by admitted data.
-/

